@namespace DotNetCloud.Modules.Calendar.UI

@*
    Help content for the Calendar module.
    Based on docs/user/CALENDAR.md.
*@

<div class="help-content">
    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Overview</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud Calendar lets you manage calendars and events, invite attendees, set reminders, and sync with external calendar applications via CalDAV. Switch between <strong>Month</strong>, <strong>Week</strong>, <strong>Day</strong>, and <strong>Agenda</strong> views from the sidebar, and use the toolbar to move between time ranges or jump to today.</p>
        <p>Work with your <strong>Personal</strong> calendars or, if you belong to an organization, switch to an organization's calendars with the picker in the toolbar.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Managing Calendars</h2>
        <p><strong>Creating a calendar:</strong> Pick the scope (Personal or an organization) in the toolbar, click <strong>New Calendar</strong>, and enter a name, an optional description, and a color.</p>
        <p><strong>Editing:</strong> Select a calendar in the sidebar and click <strong>Edit</strong> to change its name, description, or color.</p>
        <p><strong>Sharing:</strong> Select a calendar and click <strong>Share</strong> to share it with another user. Enter the recipient's user ID and choose <strong>Read Only</strong> or <strong>Read/Write</strong> permissions. Shares can be revoked at any time.</p>
        <p><strong>Exporting and importing:</strong> Select a calendar and use <strong>Export iCal</strong> to download it, or <strong>Import</strong> to paste iCalendar (<code>.ics</code>) data.</p>
        <p><strong>Deleting:</strong> Select a calendar and click <strong>Delete</strong>. The calendar and all of its events are deleted.</p>
        <p>You can have multiple calendars (e.g., "Work", "Personal", "Holidays").</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Managing Events</h2>
        <p><strong>Creating an event:</strong> Select the calendar the event should belong to in the sidebar, then click a date/time in the calendar view or click <strong>+ New Event</strong>. Fill in the title, start/end date and time, location, and description, and optionally set a color.</p>
        <p><strong>All-day events:</strong> Toggle the <strong>All-day event</strong> option for full-day events.</p>
        <p><strong>Recurring events:</strong> Choose <strong>Daily</strong>, <strong>Weekly</strong>, <strong>Biweekly</strong>, <strong>Monthly</strong>, or <strong>Yearly</strong> repetition, optionally set an end date, and pick specific weekdays for weekly and monthly rules.</p>
        <p><strong>Links:</strong> Add a <strong>URL</strong> to an event, for example a video call link.</p>
        <p><strong>Editing:</strong> Click an event and change its details.</p>
        <p><strong>Deleting:</strong> Open an event and click <strong>Delete</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Invitations</h2>
        <p>Add attendees to an event by searching your contacts or entering an email address and name, and mark each attendee as <strong>Required</strong>, <strong>Optional</strong>, or <strong>FYI</strong>. In the Agenda view, invitees can respond to an invitation with <strong>Accept</strong>, <strong>Maybe</strong>, or <strong>Decline</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Reminders</h2>
        <p>Add one or more reminders to an event. Choose <strong>Notification</strong> or <strong>Email</strong> and the number of minutes before the event starts.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">CalDAV Sync</h2>
        <p>Calendars are accessible via CalDAV, allowing you to sync with external applications like Thunderbird, Apple Calendar, or mobile devices. Use your DotNetCloud credentials to connect.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Tips &amp; Tricks</h2>
        <ul class="help-tips">
            <li>Use different colors for different calendars for quick visual identification.</li>
            <li>Use the Agenda view to see all upcoming events as a flat list and to respond to invitations.</li>
            <li>Export a calendar with <strong>Export iCal</strong> for backup or to move it to another service.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
